8:["$","section","Writing",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Writing"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":"[\n  {\n    \"date\": \"Coming soon\",\n    \"category\": \"Systems\",\n    \"title\": \"Automation vs. AI Automation — What Actually Changes?\",\n    \"excerpt\": \"How traditional automation is evolving into intelligent, context-aware workflows.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"date\": \"Coming soon\",\n    \"category\": \"AI\",\n    \"title\": \"From Automation to Autonomous Systems\",\n    \"excerpt\": \"Exploring the shift from rule-based automation to AI systems with agency.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"date\": \"Coming soon\",\n    \"category\": \"Building\",\n    \"title\": \"Building AI Products with No Funding\",\n    \"excerpt\": \"Lessons from experimenting with products, tools, and MVPs as an independent builder.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"date\": \"Coming soon\",\n    \"category\": \"Notes\",\n    \"title\": \"What I Learned Building AI Agents\",\n    \"excerpt\": \"Practical observations from LLMs, RAG, tools, and agent workflows.\"\n  }\n]"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Structured and ready for add, edit, delete, reorder, and publish controls when connected to your preferred data store."}]]}]
10:T9cc,[
  {
    "period": "2018—2022",
    "title": "Mechanical curiosity",
    "copy": "Before software, my curiosity was mechanical. I spent these years around motorcycles—restoring bikes, trying power upgrades, testing unusual setups, and learning what changes when you take something apart and put it back together with more intent."
  },
  {
    "period": "2023",
    "title": "A complete reset",
    "copy": "Health issues asked me to step away from automobiles. On March 21, I joined an institution to learn programming and began with Java. It did not click, and I stopped. In November, I started again with HTML, then CSS and JavaScript. The first attempt failed; the second changed everything."
  },
  {
    "period": "2024",
    "title": "Trying everything, chasing something",
    "copy": "AI tools became a way to learn faster and experiment more freely. I explored coding tools, React Native basics, Flutter, and software development without a neat map. I was building, curious, and still looking for the work that would hold my attention."
  },
  {
    "period": "2025",
    "title": "Business, marketing, another pivot",
    "copy": "With a college friend, I started Monkfit, an online clothing business. It taught me about products, marketing, and making decisions for real users. Digital marketing later sharpened that lens. The experience was valuable—and made it clear that my deepest curiosity lived elsewhere."
  },
  {
    "period": "January 2026",
    "title": "One last dance",
    "copy": "I made a serious promise to myself: one final, focused attempt. I began with Python and, for the first time, the work felt different. It led me into AI, Generative AI, automation, RAG, and the patient craft of building systems.",
    "feature": true
  },
  {
    "period": "2026",
    "title": "Going deeper into AI",
    "copy": "I joined a Generative AI course at IIT Madras and learned with the guidance of five mentors. The experience helped turn tool-assisted experimentation into a more structured understanding of Generative AI, automation, RAG, AI agents, machine learning, and deep learning."
  },
  {
    "period": "Present",
    "title": "Zcloud Digitech",
    "copy": "I am building Zcloud Digitech, working on freelance projects, and continuing to experiment with emerging technology. AI, automation, mathematics, physics, and intelligent systems are all part of the current exploration. I am still learning. Still building. Still experimenting. This is only the beginning."
  }
